    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup for LawDog presents a clear path to offensive production, headlined by **Tyler Freeman** (72.83) and **Bryce Harper** (71.47), our two strongest plays. **Tyler Freeman** benefits from a massive 14% park adjustment and a 17% boost against a struggling Miles Mikolas, while the wind blowing out adds critical upside to his profile. **Bryce Harper** remains an anchor in the #3 hole, capitalizing on a favorable matchup against Justin Wrobleski and positive wind conditions that should help him drive the ball. **Luis Arraez** (69.53) and **Jung Hoo Lee** (65.93) are also high-floor options today, both exploiting the lack of command from Luinder Avila; their high contact rates against a weak arm make them essential for stabilizing our batting average category.\n\nWe are navigating a few situational risks, primarily with **Gleyber Torres** (64.48) and **Tyler Freeman**, both of whom are currently facing potential rain delays. While **Gleyber Torres** holds a strong score, the 41% rain risk requires a watchful eye; if he is scratched or the game is postponed, we must pivot to our bench. The most difficult decision today was leaving **Geraldo Perdomo** (51.24) on the bench. He was the primary candidate to displace **Jeremiah Jackson** (46.19), but **Jeremiah Jackson** earns the start here due to his superior park factor and the specific situational bonus provided by the opponent\u2019s slow delivery, which maximizes our stolen base potential\u2014a high-priority category for this roster. \n\nThe lineup is built to balance raw power with high-efficiency plate appearances, specifically targeting the vulnerabilities of pitchers like Luinder Avila and Tyler Phillips. **Yainer Diaz** (62.34) and **Taylor Ward** (60.48) round out the core, providing strong platoon advantages against their respective starters. Although we are waiting for official lineups, the projected order for **Jonathan Aranda** (60.01) against Kevin Gausman suggests he will have ample opportunity to contribute, even against a tough arm. We are monitoring **Cal Raleigh** (47.94) and **Drew Gilbert** (55.45) as our lower-floor plays; should official lineups push them lower in the order, we will be ready to swap in **Daulton Varsho** (49.27) or **Lawrence Butler** (46.38) to keep our daily efficiency scores competitive.",
